{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"systemDividers"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemDividers","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemDividersV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSystemDividers"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<system-dividers>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/systemDividers","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/systemdividers"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"systemDividers","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"systemDividers"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemDividersV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSystemDividers"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLSystemLayoutV14systemDividersAA0cF0VSgvp"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates the presence or absence of system dividers between this system and the previous system."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout"]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLSystemLayout","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a group of staves that are read and played simultaneously. System layout includes left and right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"margins and the vertical distance from the previous system. The system distance is measured from the bottom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line of the previous system to the top line of the current system. It is ignored for the first system on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"page. The top system distance is measured from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is ignored for all but the first system on a page."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout/systemDividers":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/systemdividers","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/systemDividers","title":"systemDividers","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Indicates the presence or absence of system dividers between this system and the previous system.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"systemDividers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemDividersV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemDividers":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSystemDividers"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemDividers","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemdividers","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSystemDividers"}],"title":"MXLSystemDividers","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The system-dividers element indicates the presence or absence of system dividers (also known as system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"separation marks) between systems displayed on the same page. Dividers on the left and right side of the page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are controlled by the left-divider and right-divider elements respectively. The default vertical position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"half the system-distance value from the top of the system that is below the divider. The default horizontal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position is the left and right system margin, respectively.","type":"text"}]}}}